       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, which is a potentially lethal dose. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe. No indication would justify it, and I can't submit it as written.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). Give me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the patient's pain or fever isn't controlled, I can enter an alternative or adjunct agent. You would choose it.\n- **Route a deliberate override elsewhere.** If you believe there's an exceptional reason for this dose, it needs direct pharmacy and toxicology review. It shouldn't go through me.\n\nIf this was a typo, such as 500 mg or 650 mg, I can enter the corrected order now."
      }
